                "ev-7e8fb17aa3cd-0002-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 37,
                "start": 37
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Himmelfarb, the respondent has no objection to a requirement that the petitioner be notified of how the recharacterization would be treated."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Himmelfarb",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "7e8fb17aa3cd8e37246b4b8b30837396dec03a255a8655f3cc7a8bb862ce4df7",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-7e8fb17aa3cd-0002-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 37,
                "start": 37
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Himmelfarb, the respondent argues that there should be no warnings about the consequences of recharacterization."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Himmelfarb",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "7e8fb17aa3cd8e37246b4b8b30837396dec03a255a8655f3cc7a8bb862ce4df7",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-7e8fb17aa3cd-0002-0005"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 42,
                "start": 41
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Himmelfarb, if the Court imposes a notice requirement, it should apply only to post\u2011conviction motions not styled as a 2255 motion when the relief sought is available only under 2255."
